00:24:52.000 --> 00:25:17.000
So, um, and it was 15 years between books, I really don't feel the pressure until I'm 60. Helen Ellis, speaking with producer Maggie Pendman. Many of us feel stuck. Stuck at work, stuck in the wrong city, stuck in life. When that happens, we often end up asking ourselves, what should I do? Where should I live? What's my ideal life?
所以，嗯，两本书之间隔了15年，在我60岁之前，我真的感受不到什么压力。海伦·埃利斯在与制作人玛吉·彭曼交谈。我们许多人都感到卡在原地。困在工作中，困在错误的城市里，困在生活中。当这种情况发生时，我们最终往往会问自己：我该做什么？我该住在哪里？我理想的生活是什么样的？

51
00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:48.000
It turns out these normal questions are counterproductive to getting us unstuck. They place an unbearable pressure on us, the pressure to know how things are supposed to turn out. The next time that happens to you, think of your life, the way a designer at a tech company, things of a new product. You don't quite know what you want to build. Just for fun, you come up with a prototype, then a second and a third. You pay attention to whether you enjoy building one kind of prototype or another.
事实证明，这些常规问题对我们摆脱困境适得其反。它们给我们施加了无法承受的压力，即必须知道事情将如何发展的压力。下一次当你遇到这种情况时，试着用科技公司设计师看待新产品的方式来思考你的人生。你并不完全清楚自己想打造什么。只是为了好玩，你先做一个原型，然后是第二个和第三个。你留意自己是更享受打造某一种原型还是另一种。

